ctoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -6)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7358f48c44a6e848b459e480d470fb76ec9957b59abeb9cb4b826a20a1718df3"} {"question" "q-90705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$-2$ or $12$"] ["text" "$-3$ or $8$"] ["text" "$-4$ or $6$"] ["text" "$-6$ or $4$"] ["text" "$-8$ or $3$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$-4$ or $6$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-6y=0$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8f116e"} {"question" "q-90706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7358f48c44a6e848b459e480d470fb76ec9957b59abeb9cb4b826a20a1718df3"} {"question" "q-90706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063643/state.json" "file_sha256" "caef25b9f18f90f83779c133e43ee6325e9f751b5be7c3b364830cdabd8